# Semantic-CV

Semantic‑CV is a structured, schema.org‑based approach to writing and publishing your CV. Instead of wrestling with layout tools, you describe yourself as JSON, and Semantic‑CV takes care of rendering, validation, and publishing.

## The CLI helps you:
- Create and edit your CV as valid [`schema.org/Person`][schema] JSON
- Analyze and validate your data
- Normalize fields to match the schema
- Render your CV as HTML and ATS‑friendly text
- Use any of the included free themes

If you prefer a fully hosted workflow, you can publish your CV directly to semantic.cv.

Semantic‑CV watches your repository for changes. Whenever you push an update, your published CV is automatically rebuilt and redeployed.

## Themes

Themes control the visual presentation of your CV. Semantic‑CV includes several free themes, each with its own layout, typography, and personality.


