## Why JSONLD?


---
Semantic-CV consists of two parts - a CLI and this website.

The CLI is a simple tool intended to assist you in writing your CV as schema.org/Person JSON. It provides commands for adding parts to the CV, analyzing it to make sure it follows schema.org/Person and normalizing the CV so it does follow and of course, commands for rendering the CV as HTML using any of the free themes included. The CLI renders the HTML (and an ATS friendly text version) to disk and you take it from there. Put it on your own site, print to PDF or whatever you like.

OR

You can publish it to this web site by

1. Installing the [Semantic-CV GitHub App][install]
2. Pushing it to a repository you've given the app access to

After a few seconds your CV will be available at https://semantic.cv/\<your-github-username\>.

By default your CV will be rendered with a [default theme][default] but you can specify which theme to use by adding `@theme` to your JSON.

Example:

```json
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  "@theme": "boiling-diesel",
  ... more fields
}
```

You can see available themes in the [Theme Gallery][gallery]

[schema]: https://schema.org/Person
[install]: https://github.com/apps/semantic-cv/installations/new
[gallery]: https://semantic.cv/themes
[default]: https://semantic.cv/preview?theme=minimal
